  "4. Confirm whether authoritative=True only replaces edges with the exact same (from, to, name) key...": {
    "text": "`authoritative=True` does **not** use a literal `(from, to, name)` key. `add_edge` uses `key = tuple(sorted([a, b]) + [route_name])`, so the identity is the unordered planet pair plus the exact route name string; directional `from`/`to` order in the stored record is whatever `add_edge(a,b,...)` passed in. Authoritative writes always assign `edges_map[key]`. Non-authoritative writes keep an existing edge if its `travelTimeBase` is already <= the candidate."
  },
